w a loading indicator while data is being fetched/processed\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If an operation takes unusually long or times out, the loading state resolves to an error state rather than hanging indefinitely\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed async operation shows a visible loading indicator while in progress, and resolves to success/error/empty state afterward.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can navigate to and use: sign in, forgot password, reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list, invoice detail, saved basket templates, account/company details, delivery addresses\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"These screens are accessible only to authenticated customer users (except sign in/forgot/reset password which are pre-auth)\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 16 listed customer screens must exist as distinct, navigable pages in the delivered product.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can navigate to and use: staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list, customer detail, customer orders, customer invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"These screens require staff (or higher) authentication; customer users cannot access them\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 11 listed staff screens must exist and be accessible only to staff role.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Admin can navigate to and use: admin dashboard, users, user detail, customers, customer detail, products, product editor, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, price list editor, system/import status, audit history\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"These screens require admin-level authentication; staff and customer users cannot access them\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All 13 listed admin screens must exist and be restricted to admin role only.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order progresses through statuses: Received → Confirmed → Picking → Out for Delivery → Delivered → Invoice Created\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order transitioning to Delivered automatically triggers invoice creation\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order can transition from Received directly to Cancelled (customer-initiated, before confirmation)\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order cannot be cancelled by customer once in Confirmed or later status\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can reject/cancel an order per business rules even outside the customer-cancel window (exact rules open)\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Any attempted status transition outside the defined sequence is rejected\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Order status transitions strictly follow the documented sequence; cancellation is only allowed from 'Received' state, and staff rejection/cancellation rules may add additional exits beyond customer-initiated ones.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice is created automatically when order status becomes Delivered\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"New invoice defaults to Unpaid status\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can mark an invoice as Paid\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice may transition to Overdue status automatically based on rules to be defined (e.g. a background job)\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice cannot be created for an order that has not reached Delivered status\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Invoice is auto-created on delivery, starts as Unpaid, and can move to Paid (staff action) or Overdue (automatic based on rules TBD).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System persists and relates records for users, roles, customers, customer-users, addresses, products, categories, manufacturers, vehicles, product-vehicle compatibility, price lists/items, customer price lists, stock items/imports, baskets/items/templates, orders/items/status history, invoices/items, payments, audit logs, and email notifications\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a conceptual data model list guiding what persisted records the system must support; not literal schema requirement, so behaviours focus on 'system stores/relates X'.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Backend exposes endpoints for authentication (sign in/out, password reset, invitation acceptance, session status), catalogue (list/detail/search/compatibility), basket (get/add/update/remove/clear), checkout (validate/delivery options/submit), orders (customer and staff list/detail/edit/confirm/reject/status/repeat/cancel/staff-created), invoices (list/detail/pdf/mark paid), administration (users/customers/products/categories/price lists/compatibility/imports/audit logs), and reports (3 report types + CSV export)\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each endpoint enforces role-appropriate authorization (customer vs staff vs admin)\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed API area corresponds to actual callable endpoints backing the UI behaviours described elsewhere; listed as required backend capability, not new behaviour beyond what's described in other sections.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Nightly job imports ERP stock CSV automatically\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Email sending is processed by a background job/queue rather than blocking user requests\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice generation runs automatically upon order delivery (as a background process)\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on rules\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled job removes/expires old password-reset tokens so they can no longer be used\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled job expires stale invitations so they can no longer be accepted\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If a scheduled job fails, it does not silently retry forever or corrupt data; failure is logged (ties to audit/ERP import failure event)\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed task runs automatically on a schedule/trigger without manual staff action, producing observable side effects (stock updated, emails sent, invoices created, tokens cleaned).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Product images are stored and retrievable for display in catalogue/product detail\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be stored, pending confirmation\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"System needs durable file storage for product images and invoice PDFs at minimum, with CSV/report storage as 'potential' (lower certainty) needs.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can download/view PDF of any invoice within their access\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Template branding, tax info, numbering scheme are open points pending clarification\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Portal generates an invoice PDF (format/branding TBD) and makes it downloadable; exact template fidelity is unresolved.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"65-csv-import-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import rejects/flags a file missing required headers\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import rejects/flags rows referencing unknown product codes, reporting them\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import rejects/flags rows with non-numeric quantities\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import rejects/flags invalid negative quantities (unless explicitly allowed)\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import detects and reports duplicate product identifiers within the file\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import rejects/flags an empty file\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each import run produces a result summary: records received, records processed successfully, records rejected, and error details\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The nightly ERP CSV import performs all listed validations before/while processing, rejecting invalid rows/files and reporting a structured result.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"66-csv-export-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Exported CSVs include a header row with consistent column names\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dates/times in exports use a single consistent format across all exports\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Numbers in exports use a single consistent format (e.g. decimal separator) across all exports\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only authorized users (per report/data access rules) can download export files\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All CSV exports (reports etc.) across the system follow a consistent formatting standard and are access-controlled.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"67-business-rules-summary\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users only ever see their own company's data (orders, invoices, pricing, etc.)\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer product pricing is derived from their assigned price list, not a global price\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock quantities shown come only from the nightly ERP CSV import\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No code path writes stock updates back to the ERP\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock import happens nightly on a schedule\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Earliest delivery date is computed based on 14:00 cutoff rule relative to order submission time\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can repeat a previous order to quickly recreate a basket\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can save and reuse named basket templates\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer cancellation is blocked once order is Confirmed or later\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can edit order contents while order is pre-Confirmed\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer receives notification email when order is confirmed\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer receives notification email when order is out for delivery\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice is created automatically at Delivered status, not before\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can manually mark invoices as paid\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Deactivating a user does not remove their historical order/invoice records\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order and invoice records are retained at least 7 years\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No online payment capture functionality is built\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No native mobile app is built\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No delivery route planning functionality is built\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No returns/credit-note functionality is built\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints throughout the system (cross-cutting, restating/binding behaviours already described elsewhere).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not implement online card payment processing\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not provide a native iOS or Android application\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not provide multi-language/localization support\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not implement delivery route planning or driver route optimization\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not implement returns management or credit notes\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not write inventory data back to the ERP\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not provide customer self-service returns\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not provide marketplace functionality (e.g. multi-vendor)\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System does not implement promotions, coupons, volume discounts, tiered or contract-specific pricing unless separately approved\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These items are explicitly excluded from phase 1 delivery; any related requests should be flagged as out of scope rather than implemented.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Numerous functional details (self-registration, password policy, MFA, SSO, lockout behaviour, address creation rules, category structure, product attributes/variants, vehicle data source, tax treatment, discounts, stock semantics, backordering, delivery slots/zones, invoice numbering/VAT, payment recording, email provider specifics, hosting/environments, audit retention, report revenue definition) remain undefined and must be resolved or assumed explicitly before implementation\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are unresolved requirements; no behaviour is specified until answered — flagged as assumptions/risks rather than implemented features.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Code can be run/deployed in local development, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments distinctly\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Exact deployment/promotion strategy between environments is unresolved pending clarification\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) must exist as part of delivery, with deployment pipeline between them.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify successful login, invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login attempts behave correctly\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify customer isolation, staff access, admin access, and rejection of unauthorized API access\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify catalogue listing, search, category filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired product handling, and product image display\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify correct price list application, price change handling, preservation of price on existing orders, and pricing customer isolation\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify valid/invalid stock imports, duplicate/unknown product handling, out-of-stock and low-stock behaviour\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify basket add/remove/update, quantity validation, delivery-date rule computation, address selection, order submission, and duplicate submission prevention\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify order creation, confirmation, staff editing, customer cancellation, reordering, status transitions, and triggered email notifications\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Automated/manual test coverage must exist for each listed scenario across the listed functional areas before release.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer A requesting orders never receives Customer B's orders, even via direct ID/URL manipulation in API calls\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Product price shown to Customer A reflects Price List A assigned to them\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Orders retain the price at time of placement even if the customer's price list changes afterward\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order submitted at/after 14:00 on a working day gets the following working day as earliest delivery date\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer cancelling a Received order moves it to Cancelled\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order moving to Delivered status (successfully saved) automatically creates an invoice for that order\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are binding, literal acceptance tests to be implemented exactly as written (customer isolation, pricing snapshot, 14:00 cutoff, cancellation window, auto invoice creation).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"73-suggested-delivery-phases\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No additional system behaviour beyond phased grouping of previously described features (foundation, catalogue, ordering, staff ops, invoicing, administration, integrations/reporting, QA/production)\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a planning/sequencing artifact, not a behavioural requirement in itself — no new system behaviour beyond what's described in other sections.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"39-reporting\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff selects a date range and views Orders per Day report showing date, order count, and order value per day within range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff views Top Products report showing product name, quantity sold, and revenue for the selected range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff views Revenue per Customer report showing customer name, number of orders, and revenue for the selected range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users cannot view reports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If no orders exist in the range, each report shows zero/empty rows rather than erroring.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Report revenue calculation includes/excludes cancelled orders and tax per a defined rule (currently undefined, flagged as open point).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff (not customers) can access three required reports (Orders per Day, Top Products, Revenue per Customer) filtered by a selected date range.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"40-report-filters\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"User enters start date and end date and report results update to only include records within that inclusive range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If start date is after end date, system shows a validation error and does not run the report.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If no date range is supplied, system applies a default range or prompts the user (open point, default behaviour to be defined).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Start/end date filters are mandatory for all reports; customer/product/category filters are optional/not required in phase 1.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"41-report-export\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff clicks 'Export CSV' on a report and downloads a CSV file containing the same rows/columns shown on screen for the current filter.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"CSV filename reflects report type and date range.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only staff with report access can trigger export.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Exporting an empty report (no results) still produces a valid CSV with header row only.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the three reports can be exported as CSV matching the on-screen data for the currently applied filters.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"42-audit-history\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System writes an audit log entry (actor, action type, target entity, timestamp) whenever any listed event occurs: user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only admin (and possibly staff) can view the Audit History screen; customers cannot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Admin views audit history list, filterable/sortable by date, user, or action type.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If an audited action fails before completion, no audit log entry for success is written (only failure events like ERP import failed).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Every listed event type is recorded as an immutable audit log entry visible to authorized staff/admin.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"43-notifications\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Inviting a user sends an invitation email with a link to set up the account.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Requesting password reset sends an email with a reset link.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Confirming an order sends an order confirmation email to the customer.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Amending an order sends an order amendment email to the customer.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Marking an order out for delivery sends a notification email to the customer.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Cancelling/rejecting an order sends a cancellation/rejection email where applicable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If email sending fails, the triggering action (e.g. order confirmation) still completes and failure is logged rather than blocking the user.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed event automatically triggers a system email to the relevant recipient via the configured email provider.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"44-email-provider\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Outgoing emails are sent using the client's configured provider credentials (SMTP or API) once determined.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Sender and reply-to addresses are configurable rather than hard-coded.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provider/auth/template/bounce-handling specifics remain open and not yet implemented behaviours.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The application integrates with a yet-undetermined client email provider; concrete configuration is deferred.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"45-erp-stock-integration\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Scheduled nightly job reads the ERP CSV file and updates stock quantities for matched products.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Portal never writes stock changes or inventory transactions back to the ERP system.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the file cannot be read/parsed, the import fails and an error/notification is generated (mechanism open).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Exact file delivery, format, product identifier, frequency, and retention of historical imports are open points not yet defined.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"A nightly scheduled job reads a CSV file supplied by the ERP, imports stock quantities into the portal, and never writes back to the ERP.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"46-data-retention\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order and invoice records are retained in the system for a minimum of 7 years from creation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorized users can still view historical orders/invoices tied to a deactivated/deleted user.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Deleting a user account does not delete or cascade-delete that user's associated order/invoice records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Orders and invoices must be stored for at least 7 years and remain visible to users with appropriate permission even after the acting user is deleted.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"47-responsive-design\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Buyer-facing pages (catalogue, basket, checkout, etc.) are fully usable with touch input on small mobile screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Same pages adapt layout correctly on tablet and desktop viewports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Exact supported browser/device matrix is undefined; no specific legacy browser support guaranteed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All customer and staff pages must render and function correctly on mobile, tablet, and desktop, with mobile given priority for buyer screens.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"48-performance\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under expected concurrent load.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No explicit SLA/response-time thresholds are defined yet (open point).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The system must handle expected load (300 buyers, 15 staff, 150 orders/day) with reasonable response times on key workflows, though no numeric targets are fixed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"49-security\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"User passwords are stored hashed (e.g. bcrypt), never in plaintext.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each API endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side (customer/staff/admin).\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Unauthenticated or unauthorized API requests are rejected with 401/403 responses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"File uploads are validated for type/size before acceptance; invalid files are rejected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and cryptographically secure.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Production traffic is served only over HTTPS.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Input validation rejects malformed/malicious input (e.g. XSS, SQL injection attempts) with safe error responses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Standard web security controls are implemented application-wide: secure auth, hashed passwords, RBAC, tenant isolation, secure sessions, API protection, input/file validation, common-vulnerability protection, secure reset tokens, HTTPS in prod.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"50-data-isolation\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer user requesting their own orders/invoices/addresses/pricing/users/account info receives only their own company's data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer user attempting to access another customer's data (e.g. by changing an ID in the URL/API) receives a 403/404, not the data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authorization checks are enforced in backend API logic, not only hidden/disabled in the UI.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Server-side authorization strictly prevents any customer user from accessing another customer's orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, or account info, regardless of frontend state.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"51-accessibility\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All interactive elements are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Form fields have associated labels and validation messages are announced/readable by screen readers.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Text and UI elements meet readable contrast levels.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Specific compliance target (e.g. WCAG 2.1 AA) is not fixed (open point).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The portal is designed following accessible practices (keyboard nav, labels, contrast, screen-reader structure) without committing to a specific WCAG conformance level.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"52-error-handling\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invalid login shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message, not which field was wrong.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Expired password-reset link shows a message prompting the user to request a new one.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to order a product no longer available shows a friendly 'no longer available' message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all produce user-friendly messages without exposing stack traces/sensitive info.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Session expiration redirects user to sign-in with a message, preserving no sensitive cached data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"User-facing errors across the listed scenarios show friendly messages, never raw stack traces or internal details.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"53-empty-states\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Search with no matches shows 'no results' empty state with suggestion to adjust search.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Empty basket shows an empty-basket message with a call to browse catalogue.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No orders/invoices/templates/report results show respective friendly empty-state messaging instead of blank tables.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed list/search view shows a dedicated empty-state message/UI when there is no data, rather than a blank screen.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"54-loading-states\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each display a loading indicator while processing, then replace it with results or an error.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed async operation/screen shows a visible loading indicator (spinner/skeleton) while data is fetched.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can navigate to and use each of: sign in, forgot password, reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list, invoice detail, saved basket templates, account/company details, delivery addresses.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Unauthenticated users can only access sign-in/forgot/reset password screens, not authenticated customer screens.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 16 listed customer screens must exist as a distinct, navigable page in the portal.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can navigate to and use each of: staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list, customer detail, customer orders, customer invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users cannot access any staff screen URLs even directly.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 11 listed staff screens must exist and be accessible only to staff/admin roles.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Admin can navigate to and use each of: admin dashboard, users, user detail, customers, customer detail, products, product editor, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, price list editor, system/import status, audit history.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff (non-admin) and customer users are blocked from admin screens/routes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each of the 13 listed admin screens must exist and be restricted to admin role only.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"New order is created with status Received, and progresses through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence as staff update status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Delivered status triggers automatic invoice creation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to cancel an order once it is Confirmed or later is rejected by the system.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff-initiated rejection/cancellation at other stages follows separate business rules (not fully specified).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Orders move through a fixed sequence of statuses (Received→Confirmed→Picking→Out for Delivery→Delivered→Invoice Created), with cancellation only allowed pre-confirmation.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Marking an order Delivered automatically creates an invoice with status Unpaid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can mark an invoice as Paid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice transitions to Overdue based on rules not yet defined (open point).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"An invoice is auto-created when an order is marked Delivered, starting as Unpaid, and can transition to Paid or Overdue.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System's underlying data model conceptually includes entities such as User, Role, Customer, Product, Order, Invoice, AuditLog, EmailNotification, etc., to support all described behaviours.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a conceptual data model list guiding implementation, not literal schema behaviours — no direct observable behaviour required.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authentication APIs support sign in, sign out, password reset, invitation acceptance, and session/account status checks.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Catalogue APIs return products, categories, product details, search results, and vehicle compatibility data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Basket APIs support get/add/update/remove/clear operations scoped to the authenticated customer's basket.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Checkout APIs validate basket contents, return delivery options, and submit orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order APIs provide customer and staff order lists/detail, repeat order, cancel, staff edit/confirm/reject/status update, and staff-created orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice APIs provide list, detail, PDF download, and mark-paid actions.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Administration APIs (users, customers, products, categories, price lists, vehicle compatibility, imports, audit logs) are restricted to admin role.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Report APIs return orders-per-day, top-products, revenue-by-customer data and CSV exports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Backend exposes API endpoints grouped by these functional areas, each requiring appropriate auth/role enforcement.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Nightly job automatically imports ERP stock CSV without manual intervention.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Emails are sent asynchronously via a background job/queue rather than blocking the triggering request.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice generation runs automatically as a background process when an order is delivered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled job updates invoices to Overdue status based on defined rules.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Expired password-reset tokens and stale invitations are automatically cleaned up/expired by a scheduled job.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Scheduled/background jobs run automatically for the listed maintenance tasks without manual staff triggering.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Uploaded product images are stored and retrievable for display on catalogue/product pages.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for customer/staff download.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"ERP CSV files and generated report files may also be persisted (provider/location open point).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The system persists uploaded/generated files (product images, invoice PDFs, ERP CSVs, report files) in a durable storage location accessible to authorized features.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can download a PDF of any of their invoices from the invoice detail screen.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can download/view invoice PDFs for any customer's invoice.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If PDF generation fails, user sees a friendly error rather than a broken download, and can retry.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Template, branding, tax info, and numbering scheme are unresolved open points.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each created invoice has a corresponding PDF that customers and staff can download; exact template/branding specifics are open.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"65-csv-import-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Import validates required headers exist before processing; aborts with error if missing.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Rows with non-numeric quantities are rejected and reported, not applied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Rows with invalid negative quantities are rejected unless explicitly supported.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Duplicate product identifiers within the file are detected and reported as errors.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Unknown product identifiers (not matching any portal product) are reported as errors, not silently ignored.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An empty file is rejected with an error rather than clearing all stock.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"After each import, system records counts of records received, processed successfully, rejected, plus error details, accessible via System/Import status screen.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The nightly ERP CSV import performs listed validations before applying stock changes, and reports results, rejecting invalid rows while continuing with valid ones.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"66-csv-export-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Every CSV export includes a header row with consistent, human-readable column names.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dates/times in exports use one consistent format; numbers use one consistent format (e.g. decimal separators) across all exports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only authorized users (role-appropriate) can trigger/download a given CSV export; unauthorized requests are rejected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All CSV exports across the system follow consistent formatting standards and are access-controlled.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"67-business-rules-summary\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users' data queries (orders, invoices, etc.) are always scoped to their own company only.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Product prices shown/applied to a customer are derived from that customer's assigned price list.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock values displayed come solely from the last successful ERP CSV import; portal never pushes stock changes to ERP.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock import runs nightly on schedule.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Earliest delivery date offered at checkout is computed from order submission time relative to 14:00 cutoff.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can trigger 'repeat order' to recreate a basket from a past order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can save a named basket template and reuse it later.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer cancellation action is blocked once an order is Confirmed or later (enforced server-side).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can modify order contents only while order is pre-confirmation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Email notification fires automatically on order confirmation and on out-for-delivery status change.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice is created automatically the moment an order's status becomes Delivered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can manually mark any invoice as Paid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Deactivating a user does not remove their historical orders/invoices from reports or records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order/invoice records persist in the system for at least 7 years.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No online payment capture features are present; payment status must be set manually by staff.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No native mobile app, delivery route planning, returns, or credit note functionality is present in this phase.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These 20 rules are enforced as hard constraints system-wide unless later changed.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No card payment flow, native app, multi-language switch, route planning, returns/credit-note screens, ERP write-back, or promotional/coupon/tiered-pricing features exist in the delivered system unless separately approved.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"The listed features are explicitly not built in phase 1; any UI referencing them is absent.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No behaviour is implemented for items still under open question (self-registration, MFA, SSO, lockout policy, variants, substitutes, compatibility data source, volume/promo pricing, backordering, partial fulfillment, delivery slots/zones, VAT, credit notes, payment import, bounce tracking, hosting/provider choice, pen-testing, IP restriction) until clarified.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These remain unresolved; no committed behaviour yet — flagged for clarification rather than implemented.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Code can be deployed and run independently in local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments with environment-specific configuration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Four environments (local, dev/test, staging/UAT, production) are provisioned for the project lifecycle.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies successful and invalid login, account lockout, password reset, invitation acceptance, and deactivated-account login rejection.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies customer data isolation, staff/admin access boundaries, and rejection of unauthorized API calls.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies catalogue listing/search/filtering, vehicle compatibility, retired-product exclusion, and image display.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies correct price-list pricing, price change handling, and that historical orders retain original price.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies valid/invalid/duplicate/unknown-product stock imports and out-of-stock/low-stock status display.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies basket operations, quantity validation, delivery-date rule, address selection, order submission, and duplicate-submission prevention.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies order creation, confirmation, staff editing, cancellation, reorder, status transitions, and triggered email notifications.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies automatic invoice creation, PDF generation, invoice visibility rules, payment status, and marking paid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Test suite verifies report date filtering, correct totals, and CSV export correctness.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Automated/manual test coverage exists for each listed scenario across auth, authorization, catalogue, pricing, stock, basket/checkout, orders, invoices, and reporting.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Buyer from Customer A requesting order list receives only Customer A's orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Buyer from Customer A modifying an order ID in URL/API to access Customer B's order is denied (not merely hidden in UI).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Changing Price List A later does not alter the price shown/charged on Customer A's already-placed orders.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order submitted before 14:00 on a working day shows next working day as earliest delivery date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Order submitted at/after 14:00 shows the following working day as earliest delivery date.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Cancelling a Received order changes its status to Cancelled.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to cancel a Confirmed order via the portal is blocked with an appropriate message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When an order's status is successfully saved as Delivered, an invoice is automatically created for it without manual staff action.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These given/when/then examples are binding acceptance tests for isolation, pricing, delivery date, cancellation, and invoice creation.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"73-suggested-delivery-phases\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Feature delivery is organized into 8 phases (Foundation, Catalogue, Ordering, Staff Ops, Invoicing, Administration, Integrations/Reporting, QA/Production) guiding build order, not end-user-observable behaviour.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"This is a planning/sequencing structure, not itself a functional behaviour — included for completeness only.\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"39-reporting\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff select a date range and view 'Orders per Day' report showing date, order count, and order value per day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff view 'Top Products' report showing product, quantity sold, revenue, sorted by revenue or quantity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff view 'Revenue per Customer' report showing customer, number of orders, revenue.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Cancelled orders are excluded from order count/value and revenue totals in all three reports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only staff/admin roles can access report screens; customer users get 403/404.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No orders in selected range produces an empty report (see Empty States) rather than an error.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Revenue = sum of order value for orders in range, excluding cancelled orders (exact calc rule open).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"40-report-filters\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff set start date and end date and reports recalculate for that window.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If start date is after end date, submission is rejected with a validation message and no report is generated.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Date filters apply identically across all three report types and their exports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Only start/end date filtering is implemented in this phase; customer/product/category filters are not built.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"41-report-export\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff click 'Download CSV' on a report and receive a file containing the same rows/columns as shown on screen.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only users with report-view permission can trigger the CSV download; unauthorized requests are rejected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If report generation fails, export shows a user-friendly error instead of a broken/empty file.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"CSV export mirrors exactly the columns/rows currently displayed on screen for the active filter.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"42-audit-history\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each listed event (user invited/deactivated, product created/changed/retired, price changed, customer price list changed, order created/amended/confirmed/cancelled/status changed, invoice created/marked paid, ERP import succeeded/failed) writes an audit log entry with actor, timestamp, action, and target entity.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only admin users can view the Audit History screen; other roles cannot.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Audit log entries cannot be edited or deleted through the application.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If writing an audit entry fails, the underlying business action still completes (audit failure does not block the action) and the failure is logged separately.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Audit entries are created automatically and are append-only (no edit/delete via UI).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"43-notifications\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Inviting a user sends an invitation email containing an acceptance link.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A password reset request sends an email with a reset link.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Confirming an order sends the customer an order-confirmation email; amending sends an amendment email; marking out-for-delivery sends a dispatch email; cancelling/rejecting sends a cancellation email where applicable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the recipient email is missing/invalid, the notification is skipped and an error is recorded, without blocking the triggering action.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the email provider is unreachable, the send is retried/queued or logged as failed rather than crashing the request.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Email send failures are logged but do not block/rollback the underlying action (order confirmation, invite, etc.).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"44-email-provider\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Provider credentials/configuration (sender address, auth, etc.) are stored securely and not exposed in UI responses to non-admins.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Authentication failure with the provider is logged and surfaced on an admin-visible status area rather than silently failing.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only admin can view/edit email provider configuration.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Only admins can see/configure provider credentials; the app sends via whatever provider is configured.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"45-erp-stock-integration\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled nightly job reads the ERP-supplied CSV and updates stock quantities for matching products.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"The portal never writes stock data or inventory transactions back to the ERP (no outbound write calls exist).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If the file is missing or malformed, the import fails, previous stock values are left unchanged, and the failure is recorded (visible on System/Import Status screen).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Successful imports immediately update stock visibility for customers and staff on catalogue/product pages.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Nightly CSV import updates StockItem records; portal never calls back to ERP.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"46-data-retention\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Orders and invoices remain stored and queryable for at least 7 years from creation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Deactivating or deleting a user leaves that user's historical orders/invoices intact and viewable by authorized staff/admin and the owning customer's remaining users.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Historical records are visible according to the viewer's role/customer scope, same as live records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No UI/API path exists to permanently delete order or invoice records.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Order/invoice records are never hard-deleted; access is controlled by role, not by data existing only for owner.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"47-responsive-design\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All pages render usable, functional layouts at common phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Buyer-facing flows (catalogue, basket, checkout) are optimized first for mobile usability.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No page requires horizontal scrolling or has inaccessible controls at minimum supported mobile width.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"All required screens (customer, staff, admin) must render usably at mobile widths, not just buyer screens.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"48-performance\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"System operates correctly under ~300 buyers, ~15 staff, and up to 150 orders/day without errors or timeouts.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Catalogue browsing, search, product detail, basket operations, checkout, order history, and staff order queue respond within a reasonable time under that load.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Under peak load, requests degrade gracefully (e.g., loading indicators, no crashes) rather than failing outright.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"No numeric SLA is enforced in this phase; system must simply handle stated scale without errors/timeouts.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"49-security\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Passwords are stored hashed (never plaintext) and authentication uses secure, httpOnly/secure session cookies.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Every protected endpoint enforces role-based authorization server-side regardless of UI state.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Unauthenticated/unauthorized API calls return 401/403 without leaking data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All inputs (forms and API payloads) are validated/sanitized; file uploads are checked for type/size before acceptance.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Production traffic is served only over HTTPS; HTTP requests are redirected or rejected.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Password-reset tokens are single-use, time-limited, and cryptographically random.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Standard controls are baseline requirements applied across all endpoints, not feature-specific.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"50-data-isolation\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A customer user's requests for orders, invoices, addresses, pricing, users, and account info are always scoped server-side to their own customer/company.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Modifying an ID in a URL/API request to reference another customer's record returns 403/404, never the other customer's data.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Isolation checks occur in backend logic regardless of any frontend hiding of UI elements.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Isolation is enforced per authenticated customer/company ID on every server-side query, independent of any client-supplied IDs.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"51-accessibility\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All interactive elements (menus, forms, buttons) are reachable and operable via keyboard alone.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Form fields have programmatically associated labels and ARIA attributes where needed.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Text and UI elements meet a readable contrast ratio.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Validation errors are announced/associated with their field in a way compatible with screen readers, with meaningful (non-generic) messages.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Page structure uses semantic HTML (headings, landmarks) for screen-reader navigation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Target is WCAG-AA-style practices, though exact compliance level is an open point.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"52-error-handling\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invalid login attempt shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message, not raw server/auth errors.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Expired password-reset link shows a friendly message and offers to request a new one, rather than a stack trace.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to order a product that is no longer available shows a clear message and prevents the submission.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stock import failure, failed order submission, email delivery failure, invalid CSV, and missing product all surface user-friendly messages appropriate to the user's role.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Session expiration redirects the user to sign-in with an explanatory message rather than a silent failure or raw error.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No raw stack traces, SQL errors, or internal technical details are ever rendered to end users in any scenario.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"For invalid login, a generic 'invalid credentials' message is shown without revealing whether username or password was wrong (security best practice).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"53-empty-states\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Search with no matches shows a 'no results' empty state with guidance (e.g., adjust search).\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An empty basket shows an 'empty basket' state instead of a blank table.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No orders/invoices/templates/matching products/report results each show a corresponding tailored empty-state message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Each listed scenario gets a distinct, friendly empty-state message/illustration rather than a blank or broken screen.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"54-loading-states\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Catalogue, search, product detail, basket updates, checkout, order submission, invoice generation/download, reports, and staff queues each show a visible loading indicator while the operation is in progress.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"During order submission or checkout processing, the submit control is disabled/hidden to prevent duplicate submissions while loading.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Loading indicators also disable repeat-submission for actions like order submission/checkout to prevent duplicates.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"55-main-customer-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All 16 listed customer screens (sign in, forgot/reset password, catalogue, product detail, vehicle search, basket, checkout, order confirmation, my orders, order detail, invoice list/detail, saved templates, account/company details, delivery addresses) exist and are navigable.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only sign-in, forgot-password, and reset-password are accessible without authentication; all other customer screens require a logged-in customer session.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to access an authenticated customer screen while logged out redirects to sign-in.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These screens form the customer-portal navigation; unauthenticated users can only reach sign-in/forgot/reset password, all others require login.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All 11 listed staff screens exist (staff sign in, dashboard, order queue, order detail/editor, customer list/detail/orders/invoices, delivery export, reports, invoice management).\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only authenticated staff/admin users can access staff screens; customer users attempting access are denied (403/redirect).\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff sign-in is a separate login flow/route from customer sign-in.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"57-main-admin-screens\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All 13 listed admin screens exist (dashboard, users, customers, products, categories, vehicle compatibility, price lists, import status, audit history, etc.).\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only admin-role users can access admin screens; staff without admin rights are denied.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Audit history screen is view-only, no edit/delete controls present.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Admin screens require an admin role distinct from general staff role; audit history is read-only.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"58-order-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"New orders are created with status Received and progress through Confirmed, Picking, Out for Delivery, Delivered in sequence.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer can cancel an order only while it is in Received status, transitioning it to Cancelled.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can confirm, edit, reject, or cancel orders per business rules, including at stages beyond Received.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invalid status transitions (e.g., Delivered back to Picking, or customer cancelling a Confirmed order) are rejected with an explanatory message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Reaching Delivered status automatically creates an invoice for the order.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Staff cancellation/rejection can occur at more stages than pure customer cancellation (business-rule-driven), beyond just Received.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice is created automatically with status Unpaid when its order is marked Delivered.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Staff can mark an Unpaid invoice as Paid.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A scheduled job transitions Unpaid invoices past their due date to Overdue status automatically.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Attempting to mark an already-Paid invoice as Paid again is a no-op or rejected with a message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Overdue status is set automatically by a scheduled job once a configured due period elapses while invoice remains Unpaid.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"60-core-data-entities\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each business concept (orders, invoices, baskets, price lists, stock, users, audit logs, email notifications, etc.) is persisted with enough structure to support all behaviours described in the other spans.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Treated as conceptual data model support rather than direct user-facing behaviour; main observable effect is that each described business object persists and relates correctly.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"61-api-areas\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each listed API area (auth, catalogue, basket, checkout, orders, invoices, administration, reports) exposes endpoints implementing the corresponding behaviours described elsewhere.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Every API endpoint enforces the same role/customer-scoping rules as its corresponding UI screen.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"API behaviour is already covered by the corresponding feature spans; this entry just confirms endpoints exist with consistent auth enforcement.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Nightly ERP stock import job runs on schedule automatically without manual trigger.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Emails are sent via an asynchronous queue so user-facing requests are not blocked by email sending.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Invoice overdue-status update runs periodically and updates all qualifying Unpaid invoices to Overdue.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Expired password-reset tokens are periodically cleaned up and become unusable; tokens are also rejected on use after expiry regardless of cleanup timing.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Expired/unused invitations are cleaned up or marked expired after their validity window and cannot be accepted afterward.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Invoice generation is triggered synchronously on the Delivered status change (per acceptance criteria in span 72); other jobs (import, overdue updates, token/invite cleanup, email sending) run on a schedule/queue.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"63-file-storage\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Product images are stored and served on catalogue/product detail pages.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Generated invoice PDFs are stored and retrievable for download by the owning customer and authorized staff.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"ERP CSV files received are retained in storage for later reference/debugging.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Stored files are only accessible to users with appropriate permission (e.g., a customer cannot fetch another customer's invoice PDF by guessing a URL).\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Storage must support retrieval scoped by permission (e.g., invoice PDFs only by the owning customer or staff).\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When an invoice is created, a PDF is generated containing at minimum line items and totals.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customers can download the PDF for their own invoices; staff can download for any customer's invoice.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"If PDF generation fails, invoice creation still succeeds but the download shows a friendly error/retry option rather than a broken file.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"PDF is generated once per invoice (on creation) and reused for subsequent downloads rather than regenerated each time.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"65-csv-import-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Valid CSV with correct headers, numeric quantities, and known product codes is imported, updating stock for each row.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Missing required headers, non-numeric quantities, or an empty file cause the import to fail validation before processing begins.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Duplicate product identifiers within the file are detected and reported as rejected rows rather than silently overwriting.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Unknown product identifiers are reported as rejected without failing the rest of the import.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Each import produces a summary: records received, number processed, number rejected, and per-row error details, visible on the System/Import Status screen.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Validation happens before any stock values are written; any rejected rows are excluded without affecting valid rows in the same file.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"66-csv-export-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"All CSV exports include a header row with consistent, human-readable column names.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Dates and numbers in exports use a single consistent format across all exports.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Only users authorized to view the underlying report/data can trigger its CSV download; others get 403.\",\n      \"kind\": \"permission\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Download permission matches the permission required to view the underlying report/data.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"67-business-rules-summary\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer users never see another company's data (ties to span 50).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Product price shown to a customer always derives from that customer's assigned price list.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Orders submitted before 14:00 get next working day as earliest delivery; at/after 14:00 get the following working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customers can repeat a previous order and can save/name basket templates.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customers can only cancel orders before confirmation; staff can edit orders before confirmation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Online payment, native apps, route planning, and returns/credit notes are not available anywhere in the system.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are cross-cutting rules already reflected in other spans; listed here as consolidated acceptance checks.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"68-out-of-scope\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No UI entry points or API endpoints exist for online card payment, native app-specific APIs, multi-language switching, route optimization, returns, or credit notes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No functionality exists for writing inventory transactions back to the ERP.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Advanced pricing features (promotions, coupons, volume/tiered/contract pricing) are absent unless separately approved.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Out-of-scope items have no corresponding UI/API surface at all in this phase, rather than being present but disabled.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"69-open-questions\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No committed behaviour is implemented purely from this section; items are tracked as open questions pending stakeholder answers, with assumptions noted in the relevant spans above.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"These are unresolved clarification items with no concrete behaviour defined yet; defaults/assumptions used elsewhere in this analysis stand until clarified.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"70-environments\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Separate local, development/test, staging/UAT, and production environments are configured for the application.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Production environment enforces HTTPS and restricted access per security requirements (span 49).\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"At minimum local, dev/test, staging/UAT, and production environments exist with increasing access restriction toward production.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"71-testing-requirements\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Automated/manual tests exist exercising successful and failed login, lockout, password reset, invitation, and deactivated-account scenarios.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests verify customer/staff/admin authorization boundaries and reject unauthorized API access.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests cover catalogue/search/pricing/stock scenarios including retired products, out-of-stock items, and low-stock status.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests cover basket/checkout flows including duplicate-submission prevention and delivery-date rules.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests cover order status transitions, email notification triggers, invoice auto-creation, PDF generation, and payment-status changes.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Tests cover report date filtering, total correctness, and CSV export content.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Testing requirements imply the underlying behaviours (already specified in prior spans) must be verifiable via automated/manual tests; listed here as confirmation that each described behaviour has corresponding test coverage.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"72-acceptance-criteria-examples\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A buyer from Customer A requesting orders only ever receives Customer A's orders, including when tampering with IDs in the URL/API (returns no data / error for other customers).\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"Customer A viewing Product X sees the price from their assigned Price List A; if that price list changes later, previously placed orders still show their original price.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"An order submitted before 14:00 on a working day gets next working day as earliest delivery date; submitted at/after 14:00 gets the following working day.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Received order can be cancelled by the customer, becoming Cancelled.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"A Confirmed order cannot be cancelled by the customer through the portal; the attempt is rejected with a message.\",\n      \"kind\": \"error\"\n     },\n     {\n      \"text\": \"When an order's delivery status is successfully saved as Delivered, an invoice is automatically created for that order in the same operation.\",\n      \"kind\": \"happy\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Taken as literal, binding acceptance tests for the described scenarios.\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"73-suggested-delivery-phases\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     {\n      \"text\": \"No new system behaviour is defined by this section beyond what is already specified in the feature-specific spans; it only sequences delivery of those behaviours across phases.\",\n      \"kind\": \"data\"\n     }\n    ],\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Purely a planning/roadmap structure with no directly testable system behaviour of its own.\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"differences\" kind=\"differences\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-1.52\",\n  \"span\": \"52-error-handling\",\n  \"topic\": \"Invalid login message specificity\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Invalid login shows a clear 'incorrect credentials' style message\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Invalid login shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message without revealing whether username or password was wrong\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-2.54\",\n  \"span\": \"54-loading-states\",\n  \"topic\": \"Duplicate submission prevention during loading\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Loading indicators shown during async operations (catalogue, search, etc.)\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"During order submission or checkout, submit control is disabled/hidden to prevent duplicate submissions while loading\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-3.56\",\n  \"span\": \"56-main-staff-screens\",\n  \"topic\": \"Staff sign-in flow separation from customer\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 2,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Staff can navigate to and use staff sign in as first screen in list of 11 staff screens\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 1,\n    \"summary\": \"Staff sign-in is a separate login flow/route from customer sign-in\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-4.59\",\n  \"span\": \"59-invoice-lifecycle\",\n  \"topic\": \"Automatic vs manual transition to Overdue status\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 3,\n    \"summary\": \"Invoice may transition to Overdue status automatically based on rules to be defined\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"A scheduled job transitions Unpaid invoices past their due date to Overdue status automatically\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-5.62\",\n  \"span\": \"62-background-jobs\",\n  \"topic\": \"Invoice generation timing: async background process vs synchronous on status change\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"Invoice generation runs automatically upon order delivery as a background process\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 2,\n    \"summary\": \"Invoice generation is triggered synchronously on the Delivered status change\"\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"D-6.64\",\n  \"span\": \"64-pdf-generation\",\n  \"topic\": \"PDF generation timing: once on creation and reused vs potentially on each download\",\n  \"readings\": [\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 1,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"Portal generates an invoice PDF and makes it downloadable\"\n   },\n   {\n    \"sketch\": 3,\n    \"behaviour\": 0,\n    \"summary\": \"PDF is generated once per invoice on creation and reused for subsequent downloads rather than regenerated each time\"\n   }\n  ]\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<untrusted_document id=\"request\" source=\"cli\">\n# 39. Reporting\n\nStaff can view reports for a selected date range.\n\nRequired reports:\n\n### Orders per Day\n\nShows:\n\n- Date.\n- Number of orders.\n- Order value.\n\n### Top Products\n\nShows:\n\n- Product.\n- Quantity sold.\n- Revenue.\n\n### Revenue per Customer\n\nShows:\n\n- Customer.\n- Number of orders.\n- Revenue.\n\nThe exact revenue calculation rules are an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 40. Report Filters\n\nReports should support:\n\n- Start date.\n- End date.\n\nAdditional filtering by customer/product/category may be considered but is not explicitly required.\n\n---\n\n# 41. Report Export\n\nReports can be downloaded as CSV.\n\nThe CSV should contain the same core information presented in the report.\n\nExact column ordering and formatting are open points.\n\n---\n\n# 42. Audit History\n\nImportant business actions should be auditable.\n\nPotential audit events:\n\n- User invited.\n- User deactivated.\n- Product created.\n- Product changed.\n- Product retired.\n- Price changed.\n- Customer price list changed.\n- Order created.\n- Order amended.\n- Order confirmed.\n- Order cancelled.\n- Order status changed.\n- Invoice created.\n- Invoice marked paid.\n- ERP import succeeded.\n- ERP import failed.\n\nThe exact retention and visibility of audit logs are open points.\n\n---\n\n# 43. Notifications\n\nRequired email notifications:\n\n1. User invitation.\n2. Password reset.\n3. Order confirmation.\n4. Order amendment.\n5. Order out for delivery.\n6. Order cancellation/rejection, where applicable.\n\nThe email provider will be the client's existing email provider.\n\nThe provider and integration method are currently unknown.\n\n---\n\n# 44. Email Provider\n\nThe application must integrate with the client's existing email provider.\n\nOpen points:\n\n- Provider.\n- SMTP/API availability.\n- Authentication mechanism.\n- Sender address.\n- Reply-to address.\n- Email templates.\n- Delivery tracking.\n- Bounce handling.\n\n---\n\n# 45. ERP Stock Integration\n\nThe ERP supplies stock through a nightly CSV file.\n\nThe portal:\n\n- Reads the file.\n- Imports stock.\n- Does not write stock back to ERP.\n- Does not perform inventory transactions in the ERP.\n\nOpen points:\n\n- How the file is delivered.\n- Exact CSV format.\n- Product identifier.\n- Stock quantity field.\n- File frequency.\n- Time of import.\n- Error notification mechanism.\n- Whether historical stock imports must be retained.\n\n---\n\n# 46. Data Retention\n\nOrder and invoice data must be retained for 7 years.\n\nHistorical records should remain accessible according to the user's permissions.\n\nDeleting a user must not delete historical order or invoice records.\n\nThe legal requirements around other data types are an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 47. Responsive Design\n\nAll pages must be usable on phones.\n\nThe buyer experience is expected to be primarily mobile.\n\nThe system should also support:\n\n- Tablet.\n- Desktop.\n\nThe exact supported browser/device matrix is an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 48. Performance\n\nExpected scale:\n\n- Approximately 300 buyers.\n- Approximately 15 staff.\n- Up to 150 orders per day.\n\nThe system should provide reasonable response times for:\n\n- Catalogue browsing.\n- Search.\n- Product detail.\n- Basket operations.\n- Checkout.\n- Order history.\n- Staff order queue.\n\nExact performance targets are an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 49. Security\n\nThe application should implement standard web security controls, including:\n\n- Secure authentication.\n- Password hashing.\n- Authorization by role.\n- Customer-level data isolation.\n- Secure sessions.\n- Protection against unauthorized API access.\n- Input validation.\n- File upload validation.\n- Protection against common web vulnerabilities.\n- Secure password-reset tokens.\n- HTTPS in production.\n\nSpecific security standards and penetration-testing requirements are open points.\n\n---\n\n# 50. Data Isolation\n\nCustomer users must never access another customer's:\n\n- Orders.\n- Invoices.\n- Addresses.\n- Pricing.\n- Users.\n- Account information.\n\nAuthorization must be enforced server-side and must not rely only on frontend restrictions.\n\n---\n\n# 51. Accessibility\n\nThe portal should be designed with accessible web practices in mind.\n\nPotential requirements include:\n\n- Keyboard navigation.\n- Appropriate labels.\n- Accessible form controls.\n- Readable contrast.\n- Meaningful validation messages.\n- Screen-reader-compatible structure.\n\nThe exact accessibility compliance target is an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 52. Error Handling\n\nThe application should provide user-friendly error handling.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Invalid login.\n- Expired password-reset link.\n- Product no longer available.\n- Stock import failure.\n- Failed order submission.\n- Email delivery failure.\n- Invalid CSV.\n- Missing product.\n- Session expiration.\n\nUsers should not see raw server errors or sensitive technical information.\n\n---\n\n# 53. Empty States\n\nThe UI should provide appropriate empty states for:\n\n- No search results.\n- Empty basket.\n- No orders.\n- No invoices.\n- No saved templates.\n- No matching products.\n- No report results.\n\n---\n\n# 54. Loading States\n\nThe application should provide appropriate loading feedback for:\n\n- Catalogue loading.\n- Search.\n- Product details.\n- Basket updates.\n- Checkout.\n- Order submission.\n- Invoice generation/download.\n- Reports.\n- Staff queues.\n\n---\n\n# 55. Main Customer Screens\n\nRequired customer-facing screens:\n\n1. Sign in.\n2. Forgot password.\n3. Reset password.\n4. Catalogue.\n5. Product detail.\n6. Vehicle search.\n7. Basket.\n8. Checkout.\n9. Order confirmation.\n10. My orders.\n11. Order detail.\n12. Invoice list.\n13. Invoice detail.\n14. Saved basket templates.\n15. Account/company details.\n16. Delivery addresses.\n\n---\n\n# 56. Main Staff Screens\n\nRequired staff-facing screens:\n\n1. Staff sign in.\n2. Dashboard.\n3. Order queue.\n4. Order detail/editor.\n5. Customer list.\n6. Customer detail.\n7. Customer orders.\n8. Customer invoices.\n9. Delivery export.\n10. Reports.\n11. Invoice management.\n\n---\n\n# 57. Main Admin Screens\n\nRequired admin screens:\n\n1. Admin dashboard.\n2. Users.\n3. User detail.\n4. Customers.\n5. Customer detail.\n6. Products.\n7. Product editor.\n8. Categories.\n9. Vehicle compatibility.\n10. Price lists.\n11. Price list editor.\n12. System/import status.\n13. Audit history.\n\n---\n\n# 58. Order Lifecycle\n\nExpected order lifecycle:\n\n```text\nCustomer submits order\n        |\n        v\n     Received\n        |\n        v\n     Confirmed\n        |\n        v\n      Picking\n        |\n        v\n Out for Delivery\n        |\n        v\n     Delivered\n        |\n        v\n Invoice Created\n```\n\nCancellation can occur before confirmation:\n\n```text\nReceived -> Cancelled\n```\n\nStaff rejection/cancellation may also occur according to business rules.\n\n---\n\n# 59. Invoice Lifecycle\n\nExpected invoice lifecycle:\n\n```text\nOrder Delivered\n       |\n       v\nInvoice Created\n       |\n       +----> Unpaid\n       |\n       +----> Paid\n       |\n       +----> Overdue\n```\n\nExact overdue rules are an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 60. Suggested Core Data Entities\n\nThe implementation will likely require entities similar to:\n\n- User\n- Role\n- Customer\n- CustomerUser\n- Address\n- Product\n- Category\n- Manufacturer\n- Vehicle\n- ProductVehicleCompatibility\n- PriceList\n- PriceListItem\n- CustomerPriceList\n- StockItem\n- StockImport\n- Basket\n- BasketItem\n- BasketTemplate\n- BasketTemplateItem\n- Order\n- OrderItem\n- OrderStatusHistory\n- Invoice\n- InvoiceItem\n- Payment\n- AuditLog\n- EmailNotification\n\nThis is a conceptual list for estimation and is not a final database schema.\n\n---\n\n# 61. API Areas\n\nThe backend will likely require API functionality for:\n\n## Authentication\n\n- Sign in.\n- Sign out.\n- Password reset.\n- Invitation acceptance.\n- Session/account status.\n\n## Catalogue\n\n- Products.\n- Categories.\n- Product details.\n- Search.\n- Vehicle compatibility.\n\n## Basket\n\n- Get basket.\n- Add item.\n- Update quantity.\n- Remove item.\n- Clear basket.\n\n## Checkout\n\n- Validate basket.\n- Get delivery options.\n- Submit order.\n\n## Orders\n\n- Customer order list.\n- Customer order detail.\n- Repeat order.\n- Cancel order.\n- Staff order list.\n- Staff order detail.\n- Staff order edit.\n- Confirm.\n- Reject.\n- Status updates.\n- Staff-created order.\n\n## Invoices\n\n- Invoice list.\n- Invoice detail.\n- PDF generation/download.\n- Mark paid.\n\n## Administration\n\n- Users.\n- Customers.\n- Products.\n- Categories.\n- Price lists.\n- Vehicle compatibility.\n- Imports.\n- Audit logs.\n\n## Reports\n\n- Orders per day.\n- Top products.\n- Revenue by customer.\n- CSV exports.\n\n---\n\n# 62. Background Jobs / Scheduled Tasks\n\nThe system may require background processing for:\n\n- Nightly ERP stock import.\n- Email sending.\n- Invoice generation.\n- Invoice overdue status updates.\n- Cleanup of expired password-reset tokens.\n- Cleanup/expiration of invitations.\n- Other scheduled maintenance tasks.\n\nExact scheduling and infrastructure are open points.\n\n---\n\n# 63. File Storage\n\nThe application needs storage for:\n\n- Product images.\n- Invoice PDFs.\n- Potentially ERP CSV files.\n- Potentially generated report files.\n\nThe storage provider is an open point.\n\n---\n\n# 64. PDF Generation\n\nInvoice PDFs must be generated or stored so that customers can download them.\n\nQuestions requiring confirmation:\n\n- Is there an existing invoice template?\n- Must the portal reproduce the exact template?\n- What branding is required?\n- What paper/page size is required?\n- Does the invoice need tax information?\n- Does the invoice need a sequential numbering scheme provided by another system?\n\n---\n\n# 65. CSV Import Requirements\n\nThe ERP stock CSV should be validated before processing.\n\nPotential validation:\n\n- Required headers exist.\n- Product codes exist.\n- Quantities are numeric.\n- No invalid negative quantities unless explicitly supported.\n- Duplicate product identifiers are detected.\n- Unknown product identifiers are reported.\n- File is not empty.\n\nImport results should indicate:\n\n- Number of records received.\n- Number successfully processed.\n- Number rejected.\n- Error details.\n\n---\n\n# 66. CSV Export Requirements\n\nExports should:\n\n- Use consistent column names.\n- Include a header row.\n- Use a consistent date/time format.\n- Use a consistent number format.\n- Be downloadable by authorized users only.\n\n---\n\n# 67. Business Rules Summary\n\nThe following rules are mandatory unless changed during clarification:\n\n1. Customers see only their own company data.\n2. Customer pricing comes from an assigned price list.\n3. Stock is read from the ERP CSV.\n4. The portal does not update ERP stock.\n5. Stock is imported nightly.\n6. Earliest delivery depends on whether the order is before or after 14:00.\n7. Customers can repeat previous orders.\n8. Customers can save named basket templates.\n9. Customers can cancel only before confirmation.\n10. Staff can edit orders before confirmation.\n11. Customers are notified when confirmed.\n12. Customers are notified when out for delivery.\n13. Invoice creation happens when an order is delivered.\n14. Staff can mark invoices paid.\n15. Historical records remain after user deactivation.\n16. Order and invoice data are retained for 7 years.\n17. Online payments are not included.\n18. Native mobile applications are not included.\n19. Delivery route planning is not included.\n20. Returns and credit notes are not included.\n\n---\n\n# 68. Out of Scope\n\nThe following are explicitly outside the first phase:\n\n- Online card payments.\n- Native iOS application.\n- Native Android application.\n- Multi-language support.\n- Delivery route planning.\n- Returns management.\n- Credit notes.\n- Direct ERP inventory write-back.\n- Automated driver route optimization.\n- Customer self-service returns.\n- Marketplace functionality.\n\nUnless separately approved, advanced pricing features such as promotions, coupons, volume discounts, tiered pricing, and contract-specific pricing are also outside the initial scope.\n\n---\n\n# 69. Open Questions\n\nThe following requirements should be clarified before final estimation or treated explicitly as assumptions.\n\n## Account and Authentication\n\n- Is customer self-registration allowed?\n- What password policy is required?\n- How long should reset links remain valid?\n- How long should invitations remain valid?\n- Is MFA required?\n- Is staff SSO required?\n- What happens after repeated account lockouts?\n\n## Customers\n\n- What customer/company fields are required?\n- Can customers create their own delivery addresses?\n- Can customer users see each other's orders?\n- Is a customer account manager role required?\n\n## Catalogue\n\n- Are categories flat or hierarchical?\n- What product attributes are required?\n- Are products allowed to have variants?\n- Are substitute products required?\n- Are discontinued products searchable?\n\n## Vehicle Compatibility\n\n- Where does compatibility data come from?\n- Is there a third-party vehicle database?\n- How is compatibility data imported?\n- How frequently does compatibility data change?\n- How precise does vehicle matching need to be?\n\n## Pricing\n\n- Are prices tax-inclusive or tax-exclusive?\n- Are discounts required?\n- Is volume pricing required?\n- Are promotional prices required?\n- Are price effective dates required?\n- Can a customer have multiple price lists?\n- Does pricing vary by delivery location?\n\n## Stock\n\n- What is the ERP?\n- How is the nightly CSV delivered?\n- What is the exact CSV schema?\n- What does \"low stock\" mean?\n- Are reserved quantities included?\n- Can customers order out-of-stock products?\n- Is backordering required?\n\n## Ordering\n\n- Can customers order quantities above available stock?\n- Can staff override stock restrictions?\n- Can staff change delivery dates?\n- Can staff partially fulfill an order?\n- Are partial shipments required?\n- Are split deliveries required?\n- Are minimum order values required?\n- Are order cut-off times configurable?\n\n## Delivery\n\n- What defines a working day?\n- What are the public holidays?\n- Are delivery dates customer-specific?\n- Are delivery slots required?\n- Are delivery charges required?\n- Are delivery zones required?\n\n## Invoices\n\n- What invoice template is required?\n- Who generates invoice numbers?\n- Are taxes/VAT required?\n- How is overdue status calculated?\n- Are credit notes required in a future phase?\n- Does the ERP also contain invoices?\n\n## Payments\n\n- What payment methods are recorded?\n- Is payment information imported from an accounting system?\n- Should staff manually mark all payments?\n\n## Email\n\n- What provider is used?\n- SMTP or API?\n- What sender address should be used?\n- What email templates are required?\n- Are emails queued asynchronously?\n- Is delivery/bounce tracking required?\n\n## Hosting\n\n- Is the client's cloud required?\n- Which cloud provider?\n- Who manages production infrastructure?\n- What environments are required?\n- Is a staging environment required?\n\n## Security\n\n- Is MFA required?\n- Is penetration testing required?\n- Are there specific compliance requirements?\n- What audit-log retention is required?\n- Are IP restrictions required for staff?\n\n## Reporting\n\n- What exactly counts as revenue?\n- Are taxes included?\n- Are cancelled orders excluded?\n- Are reports required in real time?\n- What additional filters are required?\n\n---\n\n# 70. Environments\n\nThe expected environments are likely:\n\n- Local development.\n- Development/test.\n- Staging/UAT.\n- Production.\n\nThe exact deployment strategy is not yet defined.\n\n---\n\n# 71. Testing Requirements\n\nThe project should include testing for:\n\n## Authentication\n\n- Successful login.\n- Invalid login.\n- Account lockout.\n- Password reset.\n- Invitation acceptance.\n- Deactivated accounts.\n\n## Authorization\n\n- Customer isolation.\n- Staff access.\n- Admin access.\n- Unauthorized API access.\n\n## Catalogue\n\n- Product listing.\n- Search.\n- Category filtering.\n- Vehicle compatibility.\n- Retired products.\n- Product images.\n\n## Pricing\n\n- Correct price list.\n- Price changes.\n- Existing order price preservation.\n- Customer isolation.\n\n## Stock\n\n- Valid import.\n- Invalid import.\n- Duplicate products.\n- Unknown products.\n- Out-of-stock products.\n- Low-stock status.\n\n## Basket and Checkout\n\n- Add/remove/update.\n- Quantity validation.\n- Delivery-date rules.\n- Address selection.\n- Order submission.\n- Duplicate submission prevention.\n\n## Orders\n\n- Order creation.\n- Confirmation.\n- Staff editing.\n- Customer cancellation.\n- Reordering.\n- Status transitions.\n- Email notifications.\n\n## Invoices\n\n- Automatic invoice creation.\n- Invoice PDF.\n- Invoice visibility.\n- Payment status.\n- Marking invoice paid.\n\n## Reporting\n\n- Date filtering.\n- Correct totals.\n- CSV exports.\n\n---\n\n# 72. Acceptance Criteria Examples\n\n## Customer Isolation\n\nGiven a buyer belongs to Customer A,\n\nWhen they request orders,\n\nThen only Customer A's orders are returned.\n\nThey must not be able to retrieve Customer B's orders by modifying an ID in a URL or API request.\n\n---\n\n## Customer Pricing\n\nGiven Customer A is assigned Price List A,\n\nWhen Customer A views Product X,\n\nThen the price from Price List A is displayed.\n\nIf the price list changes later, previously placed orders retain their original price.\n\n---\n\n## Delivery Date\n\nGiven the current day is a working day:\n\n- An order submitted before 14:00 gets the next working day as the earliest delivery date.\n- An order submitted at or after 14:00 gets the following working day as the earliest delivery date.\n\n---\n\n## Order Cancellation\n\nGiven an order has status `Received`,\n\nWhen the customer cancels it,\n\nThen the order becomes `Cancelled`.\n\nGiven an order has status `Confirmed`,\n\nWhen the customer attempts to cancel it,\n\nThen cancellation through the portal is not allowed.\n\n---\n\n## Invoice Creation\n\nGiven an order is marked `Delivered`,\n\nWhen the delivery status is successfully saved,\n\nThen an invoice is automatically created for that order.\n\n---\n\n# 73. Suggested Delivery Phases\n\nThe following is a planning structure only and should not be treated as an estimate.\n\n## Phase 1 — Foundation\n\n- Project setup.\n- Authentication.\n- User roles.\n- Database.\n- Base application layout.\n- Environment configuration.\n- CI/CD foundation.\n\n## Phase 2 — Customer Catalogue\n\n- Product catalogue.\n- Categories.\n- Search.\n- Product detail.\n- Customer pricing.\n- Stock display.\n\n## Phase 3 — Ordering\n\n- Basket.\n- Checkout.\n- Delivery dates.\n- Addresses.\n- Order creation.\n- Order history.\n- Repeat orders.\n- Basket templates.\n\n## Phase 4 — Staff Operations\n\n- Staff dashboard.\n- Order queue.\n- Order editing.\n- Order confirmation.\n- Order cancellation/rejection.\n- Staff-created orders.\n- Delivery export.\n\n## Phase 5 — Invoicing\n\n- Invoice generation.\n- Invoice list.\n- Invoice details.\n- PDF generation.\n- Payment status.\n- Staff payment recording.\n\n## Phase 6 — Administration\n\n- Product management.\n- Categories.\n- Price lists.\n- Customer management.\n- User management.\n- Vehicle compatibility.\n\n## Phase 7 — Integrations and Reporting\n\n- ERP stock import.\n- Email integration.\n- Reports.\n- CSV exports.\n- Audit logs.\n\n## Phase 8 — QA and Production\n\n- Integration testing.\n- Security testing.\n- Regression testing.\n- UAT.\n- Production deployment.\n- Monitoring.\n- Documentation.\n\n---\n\n</untrusted_document>\n\nList the questions."}